  "name": "Question 19",
  "problem": "If $A={4,8}$ and $B={x,y,z},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times (A\\times B)?$\n\n- $(4,(8,z))$\n- $(8,(8,x))$\n- $(8,4,y)$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times B$ consists of every combination of ${4,8}$ with ${x,y,z},$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/72feee192b949dcce7b0f10f4e1d772c809bcf73de6c66f15c7de75a4a1ff672.png)\n\nHence, the set $A\\times B$ is given by\n\n$$\nA\\times B={(4,x),(4,y),(4,z),(8,x),(8,y),(8,z)}.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian product\n\n$$\nA\\times (A\\times B)\n$$\n\nconsists of every combination of $A$ and $A\\times B,$ as shown in the schematic below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040355/assets/1ae41857d4aee82a2a4ad838c20bbe72b05a1505a5f4df3aa4a86fda0fff0612.png)\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n|A\\times (A\\times B)|=|A|\\cdot |A\\times B|=2\\cdot 6=12.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(4,(8,z))$ and $(8,(8,x))$ are in $A\\times \\text{\\(}A\\times B).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
